WEBVTT

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:03.980
I don't believe this!

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.730
The White Blood Cells
are nowhere to be seen!

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:10.070
Just what in the world...

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:15.990
WHITE BLOOD CELL

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.280
is happening to this body?

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.960
EPISODE 9:
CALAMITY, ATHLETE'S FOOT,
AND THE MEANING
OF WORK

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:54.420
Yo!

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:57.090
Oh. Thank you for your hard work.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:58.430
Where are you headed now?

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:02.260
First the testes, then I'm dropping by the thighs,
then the Achilles' tendons,

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:04.560
and then I'll be passing
through the calves to get back here.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.350
Talk about peak productivity!

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.350
I guess you've overtaken me
in terms of workload, huh?

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:10.810
Oh no, of course not.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:17.320
All jokes aside, you and your generation will be
supporting this body. I know you're up to it.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.450
Right.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:28.330
Come to think of it...

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:31.330
we haven't caused
any erections lately, have we?

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.840
It must be because the blood vessels
are constricted due to stress,

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.130
and there isn't enough blood flow
to the area.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:40.220
I remember when it used to be
a daily morning ritual.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:43.050
What? Every morning doesn't sound
like the right timing.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:46.140
<i>Nocturnal penile tumescence.</i>

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.560
<i>A maintenance process for erections</i>

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:53.020
<i>caused by a regular supply of blood
to the testicles while sleeping.</i>

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.770
<i>Also known as "morning wood."</i>

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:57.030
<i>Not caused by the urge to urinate.</i>

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.700
Huh? What are those things?

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:05.370
Those are ringworms. They're just low-level scrubs
that won't do much damage if we ignore them.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:06.990
Ringworms...

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:09.410
<i>Ringworm.</i>

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:13.580
<i>A type of mold, a fungus
prevalent in the natural world.</i>

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:17.510
<i>They invade through the skin's cuticles
and cause itching and the like.</i>

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:20.170
<i>They thrive in hot, moist environments.</i>

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.140
We don't usually see them
all the way out here.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.220
What are the White Blood Cells doing?

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.390
I've come to deliver your oxygen!

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.820
Excuse me!

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.190
Huh?

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.660
But there were tons
of spermatogonia here before.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.080
How did this happen?

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.000
Smoking, alcohol...

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.920
low testosterone levels due to stress...
That's what caused this.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.630
Sertoli Cell?

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.500
<i>Sertoli Cells.</i>

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:03.090
<i>They support and provide nourishment
to the spermatogonia in the testes.</i>

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:07.350
There's been a significant drop in numbers,
and they all seem listless.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.560
Then, what about the goal
of leaving behind descendants?

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.270
It just can't handle that right now.
Not this body.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:34.000
Good work!

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.750
Oh hey, good work.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:40.920
Hey, come on, what gives? What's with that
blatantly depressed look on your face?

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:44.380
Well, I'm wondering
what's going to become of this body.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:45.090
Huh?

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:46.970
Can't you sense it?

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:51.560
Lately, no matter where you go, everyone's
wiped out, and there are less and less of them.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.230
You know, like when we went
to the liver recently.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:55.350
LIVER

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:01.110
We've got to work harder.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:06.410
It's up to us to run around like crazy
and deliver more fresh oxygen.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.490
Or this body's only going to get worse.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:11.870
Hey, that's not just on us, you know.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.080
You seem to have a lot of energy today.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.830
Huh? You think so?

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:20.210
Don't tell me you had
another energy drink.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.590
I'm telling you, I haven't!

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.300
Wh-White Blood Cell?

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.590
You guys, have you seen
the other White Blood Cells?

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:29.640
Huh?

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.770
Now that you mention it,
I've been all over,

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:34.430
but I don't think I've seen any.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:37.310
So, I was right.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:38.690
Huh?

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:44.400
The White Blood Cell count
is severely depleted!

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:48.530
But I'm sure they were plentiful
until quite recently.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:53.660
It seemed that way because of
a temporary surge of White Blood Cells

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:56.790
sent in to fight the germs
that increased due to stress.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:58.370
But now...

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.540
due to recurring battles
with viruses and bacteria...

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:08.930
the number of spent White Blood Cells has surpassed
the number produced in the bone marrow.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:13.560
Either way, when there aren't enough
White Blood Cells in the system,

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.390
immunity takes a nosedive.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:19.600
I want you to be even more vigilant than ever.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:20.600
Right.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.820
I don't think I've ever seen that before.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.070
What?

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:30.110
White Blood Cell looking so grim
in front of us.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.410
True.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:35.330
Just as I thought, this body...

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:45.880
Hey, isn't that...

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.840
Everyone, these are the lungs.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:52.300
This is where carbon dioxide and oxygen
are transferred through gas exchange...

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:58.060
and oxygen is delivered to the body's cells.
That's the basic workflow.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:00.850
Hey, that's rookie training, right?
What a blast from the past!

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:04.020
So now, there's a whole class
of newer Red Blood Cells than us, huh?

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:07.650
Man, I've been waiting forever
for the newbies to come in!

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:10.200
Now we can hand off
all the work we want, right?

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:14.530
No, you know we can't do that.
As their senpais, we gotta set a good example.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.660
There you go again, honor student!

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:21.170
But weren't there a lot more of us?

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.500
You're right, that's a small group.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:27.800
This must be another effect
of all the smoking and drinking.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:31.760
The Red Blood Cell production
must be lagging because of iron deficiency.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:35.430
Yeah, it seems like we're passing by
a lot less Red Blood Cells than before.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:39.520
With numbers this low,
each and every one of us will have to step up.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:43.020
Isn't that guy...

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:45.520
AA2153-senpai?

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:46.480
Huh?

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:50.150
You know, the one who got
the latest Top Rookie Award!

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.150
Oh really? That's him?

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:56.870
Excuse me, you're AA2153-senpai,
aren't you?

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.740
Huh? Well, yes, I am.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:02.040
Can I shake your hand?
I totally idolize you!

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:05.540
Huh? Me? You're kidding.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:08.340
Hey, can I shake your hand, too?

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:10.130
Uh, sure.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.470
Jeez, you're like a celebrity.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:14.510
Hey, come to think of it,

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:17.600
the other day, when that blood clot got stuck
in the pulmonary artery,

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:20.560
it was you who saved the Lung Cells, too,
wasn't it, Senpai?

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:24.140
Y-Yeah. I'm surprised you know that.

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:25.690
You really turned out great, huh?

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.980
I'm always hearing
about your stellar work.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:31.900
You're the rising star of this body.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:33.900
That's an exaggeration, sir.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:39.540
You know, these kids are done with their training,
and it's time for them to go into the field.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:43.370
If you don't mind,
can I ask you to be their mentor?

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:45.670
You want to ask me to?

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.880
Oh, please! I'd love to learn
by watching you work!

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:53.130
What? I don't know what to say.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:01.890
So, what do I have to do to become
a Red Blood Cell like you, Senpai?

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:03.430
Um...

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:07.560
Well, it's not like I've ever thought
there was anything great about me, so...

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:11.940
Well, just keep delivering oxygen,
sure and steady, day after day.

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:14.070
Since that's about all that we can do.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:18.990
Oh wow! That humble attitude,
the way you don't act like a hotshot... So cool!

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:20.530
Hey, come on.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:25.580
The blood vessel's going to get really narrow here,
so let's carry our oxygen by hand.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:26.870
- Okay!
- Okay!

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:30.960
If you hold it by the corners like this,
it'll be nice and stable.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:34.720
- You're right!
- These things are pretty heavy, huh?

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.760
Well, I guess it'll be tough for you
until you get used to it.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:39.090
Let me have some of yours.

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:45.560
Are you all right?

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.770
Yeah, I'm totally fine. Let's go!

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:51.730
MUSCLE

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:56.740
Hey!

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.030
Safe!

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.740
Hey, I'm so sorry!

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:07.250
You really need to watch out
for unevenness and obstacles on hills.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.210
Right.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:10.750
Oh hey, sorry about that!

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:14.000
It's okay. I'll go get them for you.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:18.720
This one needs to go to that other building.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:21.180
Make sure you don't get the wrong apartment.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:22.050
Right.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:23.260
What about this receipt?

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:24.180
Let's see...

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.470
Hey you!

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:29.480
Do you realize how late today's delivery is?
I've been waiting and waiting!

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:32.360
Oh, sorry about that. I'm doubling
as a mentor to these rookies, so—

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:34.530
That has nothing to do with me!

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.240
You need to transport it
at the usual pace!

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.570
Understood! I'll get right on that!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:42.280
Sorry. All because of us...

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:44.080
Don't worry about it.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.370
We're out of time, so I'll take
your deliveries along with mine.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:50.330
But...

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:51.750
Senpai!

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:03.800
Oh man, I'm wiped!

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.680
I can't move anymore.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:09.440
Do you always deliver this much?

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:12.270
Well, today's load
was actually lighter than usual.

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:15.980
- Are you serious?
- You really are amazing, Senpai!

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:20.950
You even took on our deliveries,
but you're not even tired out.

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:24.490
Is this what it takes to be
the winner of the Top Rookie Award?

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:25.870
Hey, I wouldn't say that—

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.120
Uh-oh!

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:28.160
What's wrong?

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:30.750
I still have a receipt in my pocket!

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:34.040
Planta pedis.

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.420
The sole of the foot, huh?
That's pretty far.

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:39.130
Oh man, this sucks.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.340
It's okay. I'll go deliver it for you.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:43.180
No, I can't let you do that for me!

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:46.560
It wouldn't take me as much time
as it would take you to do it.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:50.140
Look, it's less efficient if I do this
while showing you the ropes,

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:53.060
so I was thinking I'd like to deliver
more oxygen anyway.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:54.810
Sorry about this.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:57.980
Hey, it's your first day. Take it easy.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:11:59.570
Thank you very much.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.450
That senpai sure is an angel, huh?

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:07.910
I've got to give it my all.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:10.370
I've got to work.

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:12.620
Yo, good job!

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.580
Oh, hey, good job.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:18.750
Hey, aren't you looking a little pale?

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:21.510
No, I'm fine.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:26.100
Come to think of it, don't we always
take a break around now?

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:30.560
Oh right. That rookie forgot to make
a delivery, so I'm covering for him.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:34.650
Huh? He's the one who forgot,
so let him do it himself!

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.900
It's his first day,
so he's not used to the job yet.

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:39.440
It'd take him a lot of time,
and that would be tough on him.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:44.530
No, don't you remember how they ran us
into the ground on our first day?

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:48.490
Well, I don't want to treat my kouhais like that.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:51.620
Not that I don't get
where you're coming from, but...

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:54.710
It's totally fine!
I'm on a roll right now!

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:57.710
And now that the number
of Red Blood Cells is down,

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:00.460
each one of us has to step up
and work harder.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:05.340
All right, I'm heading this way.

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:07.010
Want me to help you transport those?

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:08.720
I'll be all right!

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:11.600
You have your own deliveries to do, right?

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.480
I still have a lot left in the tank.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:15.480
I'll see you later!

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.560
Gotta give it my all.

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:19.320
Gotta work hard.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:29.950
Hey, hold up!
Let me give you a hand, after all!

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.700
Ugh! So filthy!

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:36.170
And it's humid in here.
Pretty unsanitary, huh?

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:38.710
What the heck is this?

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:41.750
Those sturdy walls on the soles
of the feet are full of holes!

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:44.090
Whoa!

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:46.510
Those are the ringworms
that were in the testes!

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:50.140
Ew! These things are gross!

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:52.680
White Blood Cell!

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:56.350
I got word that there was a ringworm outbreak
in the planta pedis.

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:57.440
There are tons more coming!

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:58.270
Huh?

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.740
This is a symptom of athlete's foot.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:08.410
<i>Athlete's foot.</i>

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:10.450
<i>Also known as "foot ringworm."</i>

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:15.410
<i>An infectious disease in which the skin cuticles
are invaded by ringworm bacteria,</i>

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:18.370
<i>triggering inflammation.</i>

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:22.040
<i>Results in itchy, painful skin.</i>

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.460
Why are there so many of them?

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:29.050
On top of the weakened immunity, this unsanitary
environment must be helping them to proliferate.

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:34.390
<i>Depending on the area they infect,
ringworm is known by different names.</i>

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:37.770
<i>On the genitals, it's called "tinea cruris,"
on the scalp, "favus,"</i>

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:41.810
<i>on the hands and feet, "athlete's foot,"
and elsewhere, "tinea corporis."</i>

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.270
White Blood Cell!

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:46.780
Weak-looking germs like these
should be easy, right?

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.780
They all ganged up on us!

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.290
Whoa!

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.080
Just what I expected of you,
White Blood Cell!

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:59.330
Looking good! Get them all!

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:04.880
Detecting scores of ringworms
in the planta pedis! We're way outnumbered!

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:07.840
D-Damn! Where are
the White Blood Cell reinforcements?

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:09.720
They've just arrived!

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:11.430
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.890
The soles of the feet were so far away!

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:15.600
You guys!

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:18.140
It's only you two?

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:20.520
We did a lot of searching ourselves...

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:22.810
...but our friends are nowhere to be found.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:25.730
Is that all we have...

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:27.900
to take on that swarm?

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:29.610
Come on!

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:30.240
Right!

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:36.990
No matter how many we slash...

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:39.460
These guys are seriously creepy!

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:42.750
There are way too many of them!

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:44.790
White Blood Cell, you should run!

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:47.460
White Blood Cell!

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.640
What's that sound?

00:15:57.350 --> 00:16:00.140
The ringworms are getting washed away!

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:00.850
What?

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:10.650
Are you okay, White Blood Cell?

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:14.530
Something's coming out!

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:21.210
Butenafine hydrochloride
is now permeating the cuticles from outside!

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:25.420
It's inhibiting the synthesis of ergosterol
and disinfecting the area!

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:28.170
<i>Butenafine hydrochloride.</i>

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:34.680
<i>Inhibits the synthesis of substances
necessary for fungal and mold cell membranes.</i>

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:41.020
<i>It causes the substances in the fungi's cells
to leak out, disinfecting them.</i>

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:53.320
White Blood Cell...

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:59.490
It looks like we'll be safe for a while.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:02.960
What's the matter?

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:04.790
- It's not over.
- What?

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:09.250
Have the White Blood Cells in the planta pedis
move out to eliminate the other ringworms!

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:13.510
B-But they just finished
waging a fierce battle!

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.800
I know that I'm asking the impossible!

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:18.550
But now that we're
so short-handed,

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:21.930
we have no choice but to ask
whoever's left to keep working!

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.560
<i>Calling on the White Blood Cells
in the planta pedis.</i>

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:32.280
<i>There are ringworms in the testes,
scalp and nail areas, as well.</i>

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.240
<i>Please head out now
to eliminate them!</i>

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:36.160
Are you serious?

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:40.490
There aren't enough of them to eliminate
the ringworms from the body! That's crazy!

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:42.620
It's all right.

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:44.460
Let's go!

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:45.750
Roger that!

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.090
I've got to work.

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:52.960
Huh?

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:57.010
Look how hard White Blood Cell's working.

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:57.930
So, I've got to...

00:17:58.300 --> 00:17:59.510
What's wrong?

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:01.140
I've got to give it my all.

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:02.890
I've got to work hard.

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:04.600
Hey!

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:06.850
<i>I've got to deliver this oxygen!</i>

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:07.730
<i>The oxygen!</i>

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:09.270
<i>The oxygen!</i>

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:10.730
<i>The oxygen!</i>

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:12.690
That's why— Huh?

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:17.700
Watch out! Hey you!
Look where you're going, dammit!

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:21.830
Huh? What's up with him?

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:23.490
<i>I've got to transport it!</i>

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:25.540
<i>I've got to give it my all!</i>

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:30.840
Senpai! Are you all right?

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.590
Senpai!

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:33.880
Don't worry about me.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:34.510
Huh?

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:35.550
The oxygen...

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:37.510
Deliver that oxygen!

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:40.680
Huh? But you said to take it easy today.

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:43.140
As if we have any time to take it easy!

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:45.020
There's not enough oxygen to go around,

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:47.350
and that's why this body's
starting to disintegrate!

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:49.730
Don't you care what happens to this body?

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:52.400
If we don't keep working,
it'll be all over for this body!

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:54.780
All right, that's enough.

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:57.360
You're exhausted today.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:00.240
We're all exhausted!

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:03.580
Look at White Blood Cell! She's fighting
germs like crazy even as we speak!

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:04.660
You need to stop!

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:08.250
If you keep pushing yourself too hard,
you'll end up going down first!

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:09.710
Get out of my way!

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:12.500
I have my own way of doing things,
so leave me alone!

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:15.750
You couldn't leave me alone, remember?

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:21.260
Don't you remember how you risked your life
to save me when I was drowning in caffeine?

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:23.050
That's why it's the same for me!

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:25.680
I can't leave you alone right now!

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:29.310
You come with me.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:31.850
Come with you?
But I have this oxygen to—

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:33.360
Just shut up and come!

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.990
CELL

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:42.620
Hey there, aren't you going to stop by
for some tea today?

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:47.040
Hey, if there's ever anything
you want to grumble about, give me a holler!

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.120
My, my, how heartless!

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:52.630
Where are we going?

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:55.290
Pretend you're lost and wander around.

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:55.960
What?

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:57.460
Oh, that's right.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:20:02.470
If you stare at a map like this, no one will think
it's suspicious if you're standing still.

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:06.850
See, look. I'd recommend
that capillary there.

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:10.680
Like this... With a look on your face like,

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:13.650
"Oops, I guess I'm stuck,"
you won't get yelled at.

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:18.570
Right, especially in the extremities,
far from the heart, circulation's pretty bad,

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:20.650
so it'll take a while
for anyone to catch you.

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:22.780
What are you talking about?

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:26.080
I need to deliver that oxygen!
So, what are we doing here?

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:28.040
We're slacking off.

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:32.160
Are you out of your mind?
At a time like this?

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:33.920
Because it's at a time like this.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:34.750
Huh?

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:38.920
The higher-ups expect a lot from you,
the guys under us respect you,

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:42.340
and you're amazing
for trying to live up to all that.

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:43.300
But...

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:45.640
don't try to shoulder
the load by yourself.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:46.300
Huh?

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:50.270
A single Red Blood Cell can only do so much.

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:54.940
You have to relax once in a while
and take better care of yourself

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:57.650
or you're going to end up falling apart.

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:02.860
See? Check it out!

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:10.490
Even if we slack off,
the body just keeps on moving.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:14.080
Not everyone can give it their all
like White Blood Cell.

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:19.550
You have to take it easy once in a while
or you won't be able to work when it counts.

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:26.640
You really are unbelievable.
All those times you disappear during work hours,

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:28.640
you mean you were actually
slacking off like this?

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:33.100
I know how to get around!
And you're too diligent.

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:36.560
Well, I guess it would be best
to aim for the middle ground.

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:42.190
So, that's what this world is like.

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:45.490
You'd never know unless
you looked around yourself, right?

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:50.530
Oh man, work sure is tough, huh?

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:51.740
Yep.

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:21.460
PREVIEW

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:21.000
Run!

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:22.500
An ulcer's developed on the stomach

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:23.790
STOMACH ULCER

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:24.670
and the membrane's been breached.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:27.460
But he hasn't come back yet!

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:26.760
FRIENDSHIP

00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:30.010
What am I supposed to do?

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:30.010
LOSS

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:32.760
I'm still scared of it!

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.970
STOMACH ULCER, FRIENDSHIP, AND LOSS
